      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The Statement says an unqualified doubling step in the algorithm “preserves $G_j,H_j\\succeq0$.” The current algorithm Definition also admits finite arithmetic, where it sets $W_j=\\widehat W_j$ and says: “The point certifier's solution balls are diagnostics for the stored solve and do not make the rounded recurrence an exact PSD-preserving recurrence.” The PSD and composition conclusions require the exact inverse recurrence; the Statement does not restrict to that mode.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "77861b9b910f0cc29756e0052ee0074e57f85597a5269053a1d149bdb726de72"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:23:2",
      "id": "thm-newton-kleinman-exact-global-and-local-quadratic-convergence",
      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The Statement says to “start exact mode” of the cited algorithm and claims the sequence converges to $X_*$. Its current Definition takes a “finite outer budget $N$,” runs only $j=0,\\ldots,N-1$, stops if a solve does not return success, and returns after at most $N$ updates. For example, with scalar CARE data $A=B=C=R=1$, stabilizing $K_0=2$, and $N=1$, the only computed cost matrix is $X_0=5/2$, whereas $X_*=1+\\sqrt2$; the finite call does not produce a sequence converging to $X_*$. The Statement needs to specify an infinite exact recurrence with successful solves, or limit its conclusion to finite prefixes.",
      "severity": "fatal",
